    <title>Kinetics properties of voltage induced colicin Ia channels into a lipid bilayer</title>
    <updated>1998-07-01T09:41:06Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/physics/9806048v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/physics/9806048v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  The activation kinetics of the ion channels formed by colicin Ia incorporated into a planar bilayer lipid membrane (BLM) was investigated by the voltage clamp technique using different step voltage stimuli. The temporal behaviour of ion channels put in evidence a gain or a loss of memory, revealed by a specific sequence of electrical pulses used for stimulation.</summary>
